1
00:00:12,220 --> 00:00:15,223
Gyro... there's something odd about this.

2
00:00:17,058 --> 00:00:19,852
Hmm.

3
00:00:19,853 --> 00:00:22,396
Why does it sound like
there's something below us?

4
00:00:22,397 --> 00:00:25,525
There is. But what are we hearing exactly?

5
00:00:26,526 --> 00:00:28,653
- Ah!
- Gyro, it's moving!

6
00:00:34,242 --> 00:00:35,618
Aw, come on!

7
00:00:36,369 --> 00:00:39,913
This dinosaur is even bigger.
And it was a dead bear before!

8
00:00:39,914 --> 00:00:43,126
Dio's stand ability...
it's the worst one yet!

9
00:00:48,840 --> 00:00:49,674
Aah!

10
00:00:50,884 --> 00:00:51,843
Aah!

11
00:00:58,808 --> 00:01:00,517
Slip through them, Johnny.

12
00:01:00,518 --> 00:01:02,519
I flattened your body so you'll fit.

13
00:01:02,520 --> 00:01:03,813
Escape down the culvert.

14
00:01:25,460 --> 00:01:27,754
JOJO'S BIZARRE ADVENTURE

15
00:02:42,370 --> 00:02:45,747
{\an8}#10
FRIGHTENING MONSTERS, PART 2

16
00:02:45,748 --> 00:02:48,208
{\an8}<i>In a poor English farming village,</i>

17
00:02:48,209 --> 00:02:52,422
{\an8}<i>the weary people eked out
hardscrabble lives from the meager soil.</i>

18
00:02:53,214 --> 00:02:56,759
<i>Amid such privation,
the parents of a newborn boy</i>

19
00:02:57,343 --> 00:03:00,304
<i>felt their poverty
grow more and more crushing</i>

20
00:03:00,305 --> 00:03:02,265
<i>till it broke them one night.</i>

21
00:03:06,895 --> 00:03:10,899
<i>They went up the mountain,
dug a hole in the rocky soil,</i>

22
00:03:11,399 --> 00:03:14,651
<i>took the sleeping baby,
swaddled in his blanket,</i>

23
00:03:14,652 --> 00:03:16,905
<i>and placed him within the earth.</i>

24
00:03:18,364 --> 00:03:19,573
<i>With that,</i>

25
00:03:19,574 --> 00:03:23,745
<i>they resolved to banish all thoughts
of the child from their minds.</i>

26
00:03:45,141 --> 00:03:46,642
Diego!

27
00:03:46,643 --> 00:03:49,811
Hey, don't tell me
you gave the damn thing a name.

28
00:03:49,812 --> 00:03:51,480
- Diego!
- Leave it be!

29
00:03:51,481 --> 00:03:53,023
I'm sure it's dead by now.

30
00:03:53,024 --> 00:03:56,402
Think of all the babies we can have
once there's coin enough to keep them fed.

31
00:03:56,986 --> 00:04:00,281
We'll say this one drowned...
washed away by the river.

32
00:04:00,865 --> 00:04:03,075
It's a terrible thing we've done.

33
00:04:03,076 --> 00:04:04,868
If we don't have enough money,

34
00:04:04,869 --> 00:04:06,954
it's because you spent it all on drink.

35
00:04:06,955 --> 00:04:08,789
What was that? You bitch!

36
00:04:08,790 --> 00:04:12,001
How dare you look down on me!
I am your damn husband!

37
00:04:15,588 --> 00:04:16,546
My Diego...

38
00:04:16,547 --> 00:04:18,549
Dio!

39
00:04:21,511 --> 00:04:22,929
Dio!

40
00:04:27,225 --> 00:04:30,687
Drowning yourself for a dead kid,
how dumb can you get?

41
00:04:31,938 --> 00:04:35,691
I do feel so much better
without that millstone around my neck.

42
00:04:35,692 --> 00:04:38,278
Good riddance to both, I say.

43
00:04:46,452 --> 00:04:48,496
You're... you're not dead.

44
00:04:49,080 --> 00:04:51,915
Your will to live is so powerful,
my sweet child.

45
00:04:51,916 --> 00:04:53,125
Forgive me.

46
00:04:53,126 --> 00:04:55,461
I'll never leave again. I promise you.

47
00:04:56,129 --> 00:04:57,713
Thank you, merciful Lord.

48
00:04:57,714 --> 00:04:59,632
Oh, thank you!

49
00:05:04,262 --> 00:05:05,388
<i>The rain stopped,</i>

50
00:05:06,222 --> 00:05:10,892
<i>leaving the unconscious mother and child
washed up far downstream.</i>

51
00:05:10,893 --> 00:05:14,230
<i>That's where a farmhand
happened upon the desperate pair.</i>

52
00:05:15,940 --> 00:05:19,526
<i>The young woman
changed her last name to Brando.</i>

53
00:05:19,527 --> 00:05:23,156
<i>She did chores at the farm
to support her family of two.</i>

54
00:05:24,157 --> 00:05:26,867
<i>By the time Diego Brando turned five,</i>

55
00:05:26,868 --> 00:05:30,955
<i>the boy was already hard at work,
tending to the horses on the property.</i>

56
00:05:32,582 --> 00:05:34,541
Sweet child, have you lost weight?

57
00:05:34,542 --> 00:05:37,295
Go on. Then eat my food as well.

58
00:05:37,879 --> 00:05:39,755
I'm already full, Mommy!

59
00:05:39,756 --> 00:05:43,092
I got a bit taller, that's all.
I weigh just as much as always!

60
00:05:46,804 --> 00:05:49,806
<i>From dawn to dusk, they both labored,</i>

61
00:05:49,807 --> 00:05:53,852
<i>with nothing to show for it
but a place to sleep, meager rations,</i>

62
00:05:53,853 --> 00:05:55,979
<i>and the cups from which they dined.</i>

63
00:05:55,980 --> 00:06:00,443
<i>It was a life of toil,
but the two had nowhere else to go.</i>

64
00:06:01,569 --> 00:06:02,945
Stop it.

65
00:06:03,654 --> 00:06:06,824
Please, I... I don't want to.

66
00:06:07,533 --> 00:06:08,867
That's...

67
00:06:08,868 --> 00:06:10,536
That's enough!

68
00:06:11,871 --> 00:06:14,206
What was that for? I like you!

69
00:06:14,207 --> 00:06:16,792
I saved your lives, you and the kid.

70
00:06:16,793 --> 00:06:19,920
You should be happy
doing something to repay the favor.

71
00:06:19,921 --> 00:06:22,005
I'm grateful to you, truly.

72
00:06:22,006 --> 00:06:23,466
But not like that.

73
00:06:24,050 --> 00:06:26,468
You have a family, a wife and a child.

74
00:06:26,469 --> 00:06:28,930
What kind of mother am I if I do this?

75
00:06:30,807 --> 00:06:32,141
Yeah, you're right.

76
00:06:32,642 --> 00:06:33,851
Apologies.

77
00:06:34,394 --> 00:06:35,686
I misunderstood.

78
00:06:36,437 --> 00:06:38,022
Sorry to have troubled you...

79
00:06:43,152 --> 00:06:44,778
Huh?

80
00:06:44,779 --> 00:06:48,240
My... my cup has
a giant hole in the bottom of it.

81
00:06:48,241 --> 00:06:49,325
Mommy, yours too.

82
00:06:49,909 --> 00:06:51,953
How come? Who broke them?

83
00:06:56,874 --> 00:07:00,335
All right, everyone gather up
and get your rations.

84
00:07:00,336 --> 00:07:03,672
One by one, same as ever.
You know the drill.

85
00:07:03,673 --> 00:07:06,092
Everyone gets a single scoop. That's it.

86
00:07:14,058 --> 00:07:16,853
Um... my cup... someone broke it...

87
00:07:19,856 --> 00:07:21,773
Well, well, would you look at that?

88
00:07:21,774 --> 00:07:24,693
There's a gaping hole
in the bottom of your cup.

89
00:07:24,694 --> 00:07:27,864
Spilled your stew.
Guess you don't eat today, huh?

90
00:07:28,364 --> 00:07:31,032
That belongs to the owner of the farm.

91
00:07:31,033 --> 00:07:33,118
You should've been more careful with it.

92
00:07:33,119 --> 00:07:36,873
I was careful with it. Mommy too.
Someone else must've broken it.

93
00:07:37,582 --> 00:07:41,293
Really? How convenient.
What a mystery, huh?

94
00:07:41,294 --> 00:07:44,379
Best of luck tracking down the culprit.
Who could've done such a thing?

95
00:07:44,380 --> 00:07:46,257
It could be anyone.

96
00:07:49,010 --> 00:07:51,512
Could you lend us
a replacement cup for the moment?

97
00:07:52,013 --> 00:07:55,766
As I'm sure you're aware, my son and I
won't be able to eat without one.

98
00:07:56,267 --> 00:07:57,309
Sure thing.

99
00:07:57,310 --> 00:07:59,854
That said,
you will have to pay for the new cup.

100
00:08:00,855 --> 00:08:02,064
Three quid, then.

101
00:08:02,565 --> 00:08:03,774
Oh...

102
00:08:05,109 --> 00:08:07,152
You know I don't have that kind of money.

103
00:08:07,153 --> 00:08:10,072
But I can pay you back next month
when I get my wages.

104
00:08:10,740 --> 00:08:13,783
Five years we've known each other.
I'm happy to help out.

105
00:08:13,784 --> 00:08:17,996
Oh! Actually, I'm not allowed
to make you any kind of advance.

106
00:08:17,997 --> 00:08:19,790
I'm so sorry, really.

107
00:08:20,583 --> 00:08:23,710
What about this bucket, huh?
You could put the stew in here, right?

108
00:08:23,711 --> 00:08:25,378
Even if it's just one scoop!

109
00:08:25,379 --> 00:08:27,672
That's a bucket for the livestock,
you brat!

110
00:08:27,673 --> 00:08:30,300
You think the sheep and cows
are gonna want anything to do with it

111
00:08:30,301 --> 00:08:31,677
if it smells like meat?

112
00:08:32,261 --> 00:08:37,058
Now, sorry about the holes in your cup,
but you need to move out of line already.

113
00:08:37,642 --> 00:08:40,811
The folks behind you shouldn't have
to wait any longer, should they?

114
00:08:50,655 --> 00:08:54,325
Mommy, I'm not hungry,
but I just had a good idea.

115
00:08:54,825 --> 00:08:58,328
- Huh?
- You'll be so proud of how clever I am.

116
00:08:58,329 --> 00:09:00,038
We can use a shoe.

117
00:09:00,039 --> 00:09:02,542
{\an8}There aren't any holes in it,
so the stew won't fall out!

118
00:09:03,125 --> 00:09:04,794
See? Problem solved.

119
00:09:05,795 --> 00:09:06,671
Huh?

120
00:09:14,387 --> 00:09:15,596
Huh?

121
00:09:18,849 --> 00:09:20,058
Excuse me.

122
00:09:20,059 --> 00:09:22,602
Could we have some stew if you please?

123
00:09:22,603 --> 00:09:24,146
Pour it in my hands.

124
00:09:24,647 --> 00:09:26,107
So Dio can eat.

125
00:09:27,775 --> 00:09:29,151
I don't mind.

126
00:09:29,735 --> 00:09:30,653
So dish it out.

127
00:09:31,654 --> 00:09:33,114
Into my hands.

128
00:09:41,372 --> 00:09:46,377
No! Stop! Mommy, why?

129
00:09:48,796 --> 00:09:50,548
Thank you for the food...

130
00:09:53,718 --> 00:09:56,387
Mommy!

131
00:09:56,887 --> 00:09:59,015
You see? I got you some.

132
00:09:59,515 --> 00:10:00,974
Eat up now. Go on.

133
00:10:00,975 --> 00:10:03,351
Please just drop it
before it burns you worse!

134
00:10:03,352 --> 00:10:06,146
I'm not hungry, Mommy! I'm really not!

135
00:10:06,147 --> 00:10:09,984
No matter how poor you are,
you must never give up your dignity.

136
00:10:10,568 --> 00:10:12,153
What would you do tomorrow?

137
00:10:12,820 --> 00:10:15,573
And the next day? And the day after that?

138
00:10:16,157 --> 00:10:18,659
Eat this and grow strong, my darling.

139
00:10:19,785 --> 00:10:21,370
Grow big for your mother.

140
00:10:21,871 --> 00:10:23,788
Big and strong, Diego.

141
00:10:23,789 --> 00:10:27,168
Defend me from this world, won't you?

142
00:10:29,253 --> 00:10:32,006
Soon as I'm paid, new cups for us both.

143
00:10:32,506 --> 00:10:36,385
Until then, here. Eat from my hands.

144
00:11:13,714 --> 00:11:15,341
Nice and slow.

145
00:11:15,925 --> 00:11:17,885
You don't have to rush, okay?

146
00:11:22,181 --> 00:11:24,182
Forgive me... Dio.

147
00:11:24,183 --> 00:11:26,852
No. It's okay, Mommy. I promise.

148
00:11:31,691 --> 00:11:34,235
Oh, please don't cry, darling.

149
00:11:34,860 --> 00:11:37,029
I'm to blame for all of this...

150
00:11:37,530 --> 00:11:40,616
You haven't... done anything wrong.

151
00:11:41,617 --> 00:11:43,911
Diego, listen to me.

152
00:11:44,495 --> 00:11:46,788
Whenever you come close to one,

153
00:11:46,789 --> 00:11:49,082
even the most wicked horse

154
00:11:49,083 --> 00:11:51,042
heeds your sweet voice.

155
00:11:51,043 --> 00:11:53,587
Even the shyest will eat from your hand.

156
00:11:56,966 --> 00:11:58,384
When you grow up,

157
00:11:59,385 --> 00:12:01,971
I think you should try riding horses.

158
00:12:03,806 --> 00:12:05,266
Maybe that's

159
00:12:05,975 --> 00:12:08,227
what you were born to do...

160
00:12:10,438 --> 00:12:14,149
<i>With that, Dio's mother breathed her last,</i>

161
00:12:14,150 --> 00:12:17,611
<i>her life cut short by tetanus at only 23.</i>

162
00:12:21,240 --> 00:12:23,324
<i>Even at so tender an age,</i>

163
00:12:23,325 --> 00:12:27,705
<i>Dio believed that his mother's burnt hands
are what allowed death to claim her.</i>

164
00:12:28,205 --> 00:12:33,210
<i>Instinctively, he knew she would still be
alive if it were not for that man.</i>

165
00:12:34,879 --> 00:12:40,884
<i>As Dio grew up and his hatred rankled,
he made a solemn vow to himself.</i>

166
00:12:40,885 --> 00:12:45,264
<i>I will find that man,
and when I do, I will have my vengeance!</i>

167
00:12:45,890 --> 00:12:49,684
<i>Vengeance, too,
upon those cowardly thralls at the farm.</i>

168
00:12:49,685 --> 00:12:53,021
<i>They all watched her suffer
and said nothing.</i>

169
00:12:53,022 --> 00:12:55,149
<i>They might as well
have killed her themselves.</i>

170
00:12:55,649 --> 00:12:58,485
<i>My villain of a father, who abandoned us...</i>

171
00:12:58,486 --> 00:13:00,236
<i>The lord of the farm too...</i>

172
00:13:00,237 --> 00:13:02,197
<i>Damn them all to hell!</i>

173
00:13:02,198 --> 00:13:04,784
<i>Guilty as sin, one and all!</i>

174
00:13:05,367 --> 00:13:07,243
<i>Bunch of shitty yokels.</i>

175
00:13:07,244 --> 00:13:10,289
<i>I swear I'll conquer
the highest peaks of society.</i>

176
00:13:10,873 --> 00:13:12,957
<i>And when I do, my foes will face</i>

177
00:13:12,958 --> 00:13:15,877
<i>much worse than burnt hands
or a broken cup.</i>

178
00:13:15,878 --> 00:13:18,588
<i>I will rip their pride to shreds
until nothing remains</i>

179
00:13:18,589 --> 00:13:21,926
<i>and make them crawl on the ground
like the worms they are!</i>

180
00:13:23,010 --> 00:13:25,720
{\an8}<i>The Steel Ball Run is a chance at glory.</i>

181
00:13:25,721 --> 00:13:29,683
{\an8}<i>If I win, even the royals themselves
will respect me.</i>

182
00:13:30,267 --> 00:13:32,602
<i>Victory is mine for the taking.</i>

183
00:13:32,603 --> 00:13:34,688
<i>And I shall have it at any price!</i>

184
00:13:38,275 --> 00:13:39,901
Not the best time for it,

185
00:13:39,902 --> 00:13:41,987
but there's something
I need to tell you, Johnny.

186
00:13:42,488 --> 00:13:44,948
It has to do
with that writing on your arm.

187
00:13:44,949 --> 00:13:48,409
Those aren't letters like we thought.
It's a damn constellation.

188
00:13:48,410 --> 00:13:51,412
They're symbols, laid out
like they're the stars in the sky.

189
00:13:51,413 --> 00:13:53,164
It's the Big Dipper.

190
00:13:53,165 --> 00:13:55,124
I'm telling you, it all lines up.

191
00:13:55,125 --> 00:13:57,252
<i>Crūs</i> represents the North Star.

192
00:13:57,253 --> 00:14:00,338
The rest of it maps out
other points in the night sky.

193
00:14:00,339 --> 00:14:03,216
Line up those stars
with the mountain and the ground.

194
00:14:03,217 --> 00:14:06,011
We'll find the next remains on that hill.

195
00:14:07,847 --> 00:14:09,265
We have to get up there right now!

196
00:14:18,983 --> 00:14:22,903
<i>Steel Ball Run</i>

197
00:14:25,489 --> 00:14:27,323
Go, Johnny! Move your ass!

198
00:14:27,324 --> 00:14:29,450
Dio is back! You need to get farther in!

199
00:14:29,451 --> 00:14:31,160
I'll be right behind you!

200
00:14:31,161 --> 00:14:32,413
Do it now!

201
00:14:34,498 --> 00:14:36,375
<i>Nyo!</i>

202
00:14:40,796 --> 00:14:41,881
Aah!

203
00:14:46,093 --> 00:14:48,136
What the hell is Dio's ability, huh?

204
00:14:48,137 --> 00:14:51,264
He even turned a bear carcass
into a damn dinosaur!

205
00:14:51,265 --> 00:14:53,267
How should I know? Just go already.

206
00:14:54,768 --> 00:14:57,312
The Big Dipper
was positioned right over that cliff

207
00:14:57,313 --> 00:14:59,023
across the valley from us.

208
00:14:59,607 --> 00:15:02,067
The remains are probably
somewhere up near the top.

209
00:15:02,568 --> 00:15:04,235
So we'll make our way down the cliff

210
00:15:04,236 --> 00:15:06,446
and cross the valley
under the cover of darkness.

211
00:15:06,447 --> 00:15:10,450
Yeah, we'll get the remains before he does
and then get the hell out of here.

212
00:15:10,451 --> 00:15:13,244
Wait, Gyro.
What do we do about our horses, huh?

213
00:15:13,245 --> 00:15:14,579
We can't let Dio eat them.

214
00:15:14,580 --> 00:15:15,788
They're fine.

215
00:15:15,789 --> 00:15:18,166
It's us becoming a meal
you should worry about.

216
00:15:18,167 --> 00:15:21,085
Dio wants that left arm inside of you
and both of us dead.

217
00:15:21,086 --> 00:15:23,004
Think he's got enough on his plate.

218
00:15:23,005 --> 00:15:25,173
Besides, the bastard is a good jockey.

219
00:15:25,174 --> 00:15:27,384
Even he would balk at killing a horse.

220
00:15:27,885 --> 00:15:29,803
I sure hope you're right.

221
00:15:43,651 --> 00:15:45,693
What the hell am I looking at?

222
00:15:45,694 --> 00:15:47,737
Why are there tiny dinosaurs down here?

223
00:15:47,738 --> 00:15:50,698
You said they were big!
What happened to being big, huh?

224
00:15:50,699 --> 00:15:52,493
Dio must've sent them down here after us!

225
00:15:55,746 --> 00:15:58,082
They're as good at dodging as he is!

226
00:15:59,959 --> 00:16:02,919
Aah! What the... I think it just peed on me!

227
00:16:02,920 --> 00:16:03,837
Ah!

228
00:16:08,384 --> 00:16:10,134
No! They're closing in!

229
00:16:10,135 --> 00:16:11,511
It's the smell!

230
00:16:11,512 --> 00:16:14,014
They're using the scent of the pee
to home in on us!

231
00:16:19,979 --> 00:16:21,437
They were rats.

232
00:16:21,438 --> 00:16:23,816
When I sent them to hell,
they went back to normal.

233
00:16:24,817 --> 00:16:27,027
We gotta keep moving, Johnny!
They brought friends!

234
00:16:32,908 --> 00:16:35,702
What are you doing, huh?
Enjoying the view?

235
00:16:35,703 --> 00:16:37,161
No way, Gyro...

236
00:16:37,162 --> 00:16:40,206
Going down the cliff, it's... not an option.

237
00:16:40,207 --> 00:16:41,916
I need you to listen to me, all right?

238
00:16:41,917 --> 00:16:44,377
There is no way
we're getting across that valley.

239
00:16:44,378 --> 00:16:45,212
Huh?

240
00:16:51,218 --> 00:16:53,261
There's a shirt on that dinosaur.

241
00:16:53,262 --> 00:16:57,265
The villagers who greeted us
have all been turned into these monsters.

242
00:16:57,266 --> 00:16:59,434
They're climbing up the cliff so easily.

243
00:16:59,435 --> 00:17:01,269
Dio's stand ability.

244
00:17:01,270 --> 00:17:02,186
He must've used it

245
00:17:02,187 --> 00:17:04,856
to turn all living things in the village
into dinosaurs,

246
00:17:04,857 --> 00:17:06,859
and every one is under his control!

247
00:17:11,447 --> 00:17:12,698
He tracked us down!

248
00:17:13,282 --> 00:17:14,699
Easy, Johnny.

249
00:17:14,700 --> 00:17:16,617
No matter how many we're up against,

250
00:17:16,618 --> 00:17:20,246
the fact remains that they can't see us
unless we panic and move.

251
00:17:20,247 --> 00:17:21,789
Listen to me.

252
00:17:21,790 --> 00:17:24,167
Dio turned the villagers
into his dinosaur minions

253
00:17:24,168 --> 00:17:25,626
to get the left arm from me

254
00:17:25,627 --> 00:17:27,253
and in record time.

255
00:17:27,254 --> 00:17:28,546
The mutation,

256
00:17:28,547 --> 00:17:32,592
I'm guessing it's a sickness he's
passing along with his teeth or his claws.

257
00:17:32,593 --> 00:17:34,887
The tiniest scratch and we're done for!

258
00:17:43,812 --> 00:17:46,189
Oh God!

259
00:17:46,190 --> 00:17:49,025
<i>We got injured by Dio
in that shed earlier.</i>

260
00:17:49,026 --> 00:17:50,611
<i>He hurt the both of us!</i>

261
00:17:53,155 --> 00:17:54,573
What?!

262
00:17:55,157 --> 00:17:57,409
What have you done?

263
00:17:59,745 --> 00:18:02,580
That's not all!
Dio's sending more dino-rats!

264
00:18:02,581 --> 00:18:05,249
Johnny, no moving. Be still as a corpse.

265
00:18:05,250 --> 00:18:07,460
For now, ignore the bastards.

266
00:18:07,461 --> 00:18:08,711
You don't get it.

267
00:18:08,712 --> 00:18:11,130
The one peed all over us, remember?

268
00:18:11,131 --> 00:18:14,342
They're using that to track us down.
They know where we are.

269
00:18:14,343 --> 00:18:16,302
They'll tear us to shreds, easy.

270
00:18:16,303 --> 00:18:18,137
Our only chance is to fight.

271
00:18:18,138 --> 00:18:20,223
That's where you're wrong, Johnny.

272
00:18:20,224 --> 00:18:21,725
What we really have to do

273
00:18:22,309 --> 00:18:24,310
is get to whatever piece
of the Holy Corpse

274
00:18:24,311 --> 00:18:25,896
is waiting on that hilltop.

275
00:18:26,897 --> 00:18:30,109
Your transformation
seems to have plateaued a bit.

276
00:18:30,859 --> 00:18:32,986
I'm the only one who's devolving now.

277
00:18:33,487 --> 00:18:37,031
I'm sure that relic in your arm
is sparing you from the worst of it.

278
00:18:37,032 --> 00:18:40,035
Its holy power
stops the infection in its tracks.

279
00:18:40,577 --> 00:18:42,578
If we get the next piece of the corpse,

280
00:18:42,579 --> 00:18:45,499
I bet we can keep me
from growing a damn tail too!

281
00:18:51,213 --> 00:18:53,881
Too late, Gyro! Dio's onto us!

282
00:18:53,882 --> 00:18:55,675
I told you to ignore them, didn't I?

283
00:18:55,676 --> 00:18:57,218
Come on!

284
00:18:57,219 --> 00:18:58,761
We gotta go.

285
00:18:58,762 --> 00:19:00,263
Time for a leap of faith!

286
00:19:00,264 --> 00:19:01,514
What did you say?

287
00:19:01,515 --> 00:19:04,434
Show me what you've got, Joestar!
Follow my lead!

288
00:19:11,316 --> 00:19:13,359
{\an8}Why did we leave the cliff?

289
00:19:13,360 --> 00:19:16,864
We were never gonna make this jump!
It's too far away!

290
00:19:21,076 --> 00:19:22,618
You're not wrong, you know.

291
00:19:22,619 --> 00:19:24,163
The jump's impossible.

292
00:19:24,955 --> 00:19:28,333
Specifically... it's impossible for them!

293
00:19:32,504 --> 00:19:35,840
I'll admit,
if Dio were of the flying persuasion,

294
00:19:35,841 --> 00:19:37,551
we'd be in a world of hurt.

295
00:19:41,013 --> 00:19:43,764
We're not safe.
Dio's sending them after us.

296
00:19:43,765 --> 00:19:46,767
They're going down the far side
so they can climb up this one.

297
00:19:46,768 --> 00:19:48,436
Don't think about them now.

298
00:19:48,437 --> 00:19:52,065
Dinosaurs or not, it'll take them
a few minutes to get up to us here.

299
00:19:52,566 --> 00:19:53,525
That's plenty of time.

300
00:19:57,404 --> 00:19:58,530
Just as I thought.

301
00:19:59,489 --> 00:20:02,867
Sure looks like
we were right about this place after all.

302
00:20:02,868 --> 00:20:04,244
You see it yet?

303
00:20:06,038 --> 00:20:08,497
The... the sand's shifting forward.

304
00:20:08,498 --> 00:20:10,918
Why does it look like
it's flowing up to the peak?

305
00:20:11,501 --> 00:20:13,044
If you haven't noticed yet,

306
00:20:13,045 --> 00:20:15,379
it's only the sand
adjacent to your left arm.

307
00:20:15,380 --> 00:20:16,631
Simple really.

308
00:20:16,632 --> 00:20:19,091
The Holy Relics
are reacting to each other.

309
00:20:19,092 --> 00:20:21,719
I don't think that would be happening
if we weren't close.

310
00:20:21,720 --> 00:20:23,388
I told you we'll find it up here.

311
00:20:32,189 --> 00:20:34,815
These rocks coming out of the ground,

312
00:20:34,816 --> 00:20:36,317
like fingers on a hand.

313
00:20:36,318 --> 00:20:37,944
We're in the Devil's Palm.

314
00:20:37,945 --> 00:20:40,571
Where is it? We need to find
the next piece of the corpse.

315
00:20:40,572 --> 00:20:44,075
Up we go, Johnny.
You're not the only one having a bad time.

316
00:20:44,076 --> 00:20:46,453
Let's track it down
and get the hell out of here.

317
00:20:54,127 --> 00:20:55,920
Gyro, there.

318
00:20:55,921 --> 00:20:57,672
In the sand, behind you.

319
00:20:57,673 --> 00:20:59,799
- What am I looking at?
- Huh?

320
00:20:59,800 --> 00:21:04,428
I... I thought it was a statue,
but... it's something far stranger.

321
00:21:04,429 --> 00:21:05,722
It's a thin layer of sand

322
00:21:06,390 --> 00:21:09,767
outlining the shape
of something unseen just beneath.

323
00:21:09,768 --> 00:21:12,103
A body made of energy.

324
00:21:12,104 --> 00:21:14,689
It's the shape of a stand.

325
00:21:14,690 --> 00:21:16,775
No good.

326
00:21:17,276 --> 00:21:19,235
I can feel my mind slipping away.

327
00:21:19,236 --> 00:21:21,946
Do you see that, Gyro?
It's holding something.

328
00:21:21,947 --> 00:21:23,323
Right there, in its left hand.

329
00:21:23,907 --> 00:21:25,533
It's an eyeball, isn't it?

330
00:21:25,534 --> 00:21:27,327
The next piece of the corpse is an eye!

331
00:21:27,995 --> 00:21:31,081
And there, in its right hand,
the other eye! We found them both!

332
00:21:31,665 --> 00:21:33,416
Better grab them quick, yeah?

333
00:21:33,417 --> 00:21:35,793
I'm hanging onto my humanity by a thread.

334
00:21:35,794 --> 00:21:39,256
Damn it, Johnny! Hand them over while
there's still part of me left to save!

335
00:21:45,137 --> 00:21:46,053
Now what?

336
00:21:46,054 --> 00:21:47,514
Dio knocked a few off the cliff.

337
00:21:59,318 --> 00:22:03,238
Oh no!
Dio stole the eyes out from under us!

338
00:22:20,172 --> 00:22:29,681
<i>Steel Ball Run</i>

339
00:23:22,609 --> 00:23:31,785
{\an8}<i>Steel Ball Run</i>

